````

== Summary
<summary>
In this module, we covered:

- #strong[CDO] is a command-line tool for efficient climate data
  processing using operators
- #strong[Operator architecture];: `cdo operator input output` with
  streaming data flow
- #strong[Four main formats];: NetCDF (self-describing, CF-compliant),
  GRIB (WMO standard), HDF5 (versatile), GeoTIFF (remote sensing)
- #strong[Climate models];: CMIP5/CMIP6 global models and regional
  models (CORDEX, WRF)
- #strong[Reanalysis data];: ERA5 (0.25°), ERA-Interim, MERRA-2, JRA-55
- #strong[Weather datasets];: GFS (NWS), ICON (DWD), HRRR (NOAA)
- #strong[Earth observation];: MODIS, VIIRS, Sentinel, Landsat

`{admonition} Key Points :class: note - CDO is the industry standard for command-line climate data processing - Understanding data formats helps you choose the right tools for your data - CDO's streaming architecture handles large datasets efficiently - The operator concept makes complex pipelines easy to build and reproduce`

